{# narrative_engine/plot_goal — the step that accomplishes a scheme.
   Asked once per plan by PlotPlanning::Plan, first: what leads up to the
   goal is planned afterwards, backwards from it. The answer is a verb id.
   Receives: mastermind { name, standing (a plot_standing token) }, bio
     { summary, occupation, ... }, ambition, scheme, finish (how the scheme
     is meant to end; may be empty), history [{ step, outcome }] (steps
     already taken when a failed plan is re-planned, worded by plot_done;
     empty at birth), options [{ key, step }] (each a verb on a menu, worded
     by plot_step).
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state who ]
{{ mastermind.name }}{% if length(mastermind.standing) > 0 %}, {% set standing = mastermind.standing %}{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_standing.prompt" %}{% endif %}.
{{ bio.summary }}
{{ bio.occupation }}
[ end state ]

[ state aims ]
What they are ultimately after: {{ ambition }}
The scheme they mean to carry out: {{ scheme }}{% if length(finish) > 0 %}
It is meant to end with this: {{ finish }}{% endif %}
[ end state ]

{% if length(history) > 0 %}[ state history ]
What has happened so far in this scheme:
{% for s in history %}{{ loop.index1 }}. {% set done = s %}{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_done.prompt" %}
{% endfor %}[ end state ]

{% endif %}[ question goal choice ]
Which kind of step, once done, is the one that accomplishes the scheme in `aims`? This is the scheme's final step; whatever has to happen before it is decided afterwards. Who or what it involves is also decided afterwards.
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {% set step = o.step %}{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_step.prompt" %}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
